cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "gh-ci-truth: classify whether a pull request's CI actually ran"
abstract: >-
  A gh CLI extension, Python library and GitHub Action that distinguish a
  pull request whose checks passed from one whose workflow runs were never
  approved or whose approval expired. GitHub reports check runs attached to
  the head commit, and an unapproved or expired workflow run executes no job
  and so attaches no check run, which makes an untested pull request render
  as a clean one.
type: software
